{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
A[Ab]hithophel the [Bb]Gilonite [Eb]left his [Ab]home
To coun[Bb]sel the king who [Eb]wore the crown
His [Ab]words were [Bb]weighed like the [Eb]word of [Ab]God
Esteemed [Bb]by both David and Absa[Eb]lom
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
When the re[Ab]bellion grew [Bb]strong and [Eb]deep
He [Ab]joined the side of [Bb]the rebellious [Eb]heir
David [Ab]fled on [Bb]foot with his [Eb]people
[Ab]Praying for the Lord [Bb]to break the [Eb]scheme
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Turn A[Ab]hithophel's [Bb]counsel into [Eb]folly
Let the [Ab]good advice [Bb]be frus[Eb]trated
For the [Ab]Lord has or[Bb]dained the [Cm7]outcome
And the [Ab]plans of the [Bb]wicked are [Eb]scattered
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Ab]He advised to [Bb]take the concu[Eb]bines
To [Ab]show the break was [Bb]absolute and [Eb]true
Then to [Ab]strike by [Bb]night with twelve [Eb]thousand men
To [Ab]catch the weary [Bb]king in his [Eb]flight
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
But [Ab]Hushai the [Bb]Archite spoke with [Eb]care
[Ab]Saying the ad[Bb]vice was not [Eb]good
[Ab]David is a [Bb]warrior fierce [Cm7]and strong
He [Ab]will not sleep [Bb]with his troops
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Eb]Turn Ahit[Ab]hophel's coun[Bb]sel into fol[Eb]ly
Let the good [Ab]advice be [Bb]frustrat[Eb]ed
For the Lord [Ab]has ordained [Bb]the out[Cm7]come
And the plans [Ab]of the wic[Bb]ked are scat[Eb]tered
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
He saw his ad[Ab]vice [Bb]was re[Cm7]jected
And [Ab]he returned to his [Bb]home in [Eb]Giloh
He [Ab]set his [Bb]house in [Cm7]order
And [Abmaj7]took his [Bb]own life [Eb]
